        <h2>Why Coworking Matters for Digital Nomads in Spain</h2>
        <p>While Spain has excellent home internet, coworking spaces offer something irreplaceable: professional infrastructure, backup connectivity, community, and a change of scenery. Digital nomads and remote workers often alternate between home offices and coworking spaces, especially in larger cities.</p>
      </div>

      <p>Spain's coworking scene has matured significantly. You'll find everything from €15 day passes to €400/month memberships, with most spaces offering reliable high-speed fibre internet, meeting rooms, and networking events.</p>

      <div class="msv__alert msv__alert--green">
        <span class="msv__alert-icon">✓</span>
        <p><strong>Spain advantage:</strong> Spain ranks #1 in Europe for fibre coverage (97%+). Even smaller towns have fiber internet, so coworking quality is consistently high.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Madrid: Spain's Tech Hub</h2>

      <div class="msv__city-section">
        <h3>Why Madrid for Coworking?</h3>
        <p>Madrid is Spain's largest city with the most coworking options, best networking, and highest concentration of startups and tech companies. Cost of living is higher than regional cities, but infrastructure is unmatched.</p>

        <h3>Top Spaces & Pricing:</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Selina (Multiple Locations):</strong> Day pass €18–25, Monthly €250–300. Social vibe, young demographic, networking events nightly. Great for community.</li>
          <li><strong>WeWork Madrid (Paseo de la Castellana):</strong> Day €25, Monthly €350–450. Premium, professional, full amenities (meeting rooms, cafeteria, events). Best for established professionals.</li>
          <li><strong>The Commons (Retiro District):</strong> Day €20, Monthly €280. Design-focused, modern aesthetic, strong community. Good middle ground.</li>
          <li><strong>Hub-It (Salamanca):</strong> Day €15–20, Monthly €180–250. Budget-friendly, growing space, reliable infrastructure. Best value.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Internet & Amenities:</h3>
        <p>All Madrid spaces offer 200+ Mbps fibre. Meeting rooms €15–30/hour. Most include printing, mail service, kitchen, and free coffee.</p>

        <h3>Best For:</h3>
        <p>Networking, career growth, startup ecosystems, and professionals seeking full-service coworking.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Barcelona: Culture & Beaches</h2>

      <div class="msv__city-section">
        <h3>Why Barcelona for Coworking?</h3>
        <p>Barcelona balances work and lifestyle. Close to beaches, vibrant neighborhoods, excellent food scene, and a thriving startup ecosystem. Slightly cheaper than Madrid but pricier than regional cities.</p>

        <h3>Top Spaces & Pricing:</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Aticco (Born, Eixample):</strong> Day €20, Monthly €300–350. Young, social atmosphere, creative crowd. Great for freelancers and creatives.</li>
          <li><strong>Sun Desk (Gràcia, Eixample):</strong> Day €18, Monthly €280–320. Plant-filled, health-focused (standing desks, yoga classes). Wellness-oriented.</li>
          <li><strong>OneCoWork (Raval):</strong> Day €15, Monthly €200–280. Bohemian vibe, affordable, community-driven. Best value in Barcelona.</li>
          <li><strong>MOB (Montjuïc area):</strong> Day €22, Monthly €320–380. Modern, events-rich, near cultural attractions. Best location for sightseeing balance.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Internet & Amenities:</h3>
        <p>All Barcelona spaces offer 150–400 Mbps fibre. Good meeting room availability (€12–25/hour). Kitchen and drinks included in most memberships.</p>

        <h3>Best For:</h3>
        <p>Lifestyle balance, creative industries, beach access, younger remote workers.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Valencia: The Rising Star</h2>

      <div class="msv__city-section">
        <h3>Why Valencia for Coworking?</h3>
        <p>Valencia is Spain's coworking sweet spot: 30% cheaper than Madrid/Barcelona, beaches, excellent paella, growing tech scene, and friendly expat community. Often overlooked but increasingly popular with digital nomads.</p>

        <h3>Top Spaces & Pricing:</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Espacio Co (Extramurs District):</strong> Day €12, Monthly €150–180. Best value in Spain, friendly community, good WiFi. Highly recommended for budget nomads.</li>
          <li><strong>Proyecto Coworking (Centro):</strong> Day €15, Monthly €180–220. Professional, well-maintained, central location. Good for serious workers.</li>
          <li><strong>The Spot (Ruzafa):</strong> Day €14, Monthly €160–200. Trendy neighborhood, artistic vibe, social events. Best for creative workers.</li>
          <li><strong>Nest Valencia (El Carme):</strong> Day €13, Monthly €140–170. Startup-friendly, mentoring programs, lowest prices. Best for entrepreneurs.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Internet & Amenities:</h3>
        <p>All offer 100–300 Mbps fibre. Meeting rooms available but may be smaller than Madrid/Barcelona. All include kitchen and basic amenities.</p>

        <h3>Best For:</h3>
        <p>Budget-conscious nomads, emerging tech scene, beach lifestyle, underrated cities seeking relaxed coworking.</p>
