      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="msv__faq-list">
        <details>
          <summary>Should I commit to a 6-month or 12-month membership?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Only if you're certain you'll stay. Month-to-month is safer for nomads—you maintain flexibility. Long-term discounts (10–20%) are tempting but risky if circumstances change. Test day passes first.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I use a coworking address for official business registration?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Some spaces allow this; others don't. Ask explicitly before assuming. If they offer "virtual office" services, address usage is usually included. Many freelancers use this to avoid home business registration complications.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What's the difference between a shared desk and a dedicated desk?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Shared (hot desking): You get any available desk daily. Cheaper (30–50% less). Flexible but less organized. Dedicated: Your personal desk reserved daily. More expensive but better for focus and storing personal items.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do all Spanish coworking spaces have the same WiFi quality?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>No. Major cities have consistently good fiber (200+ Mbps). Smaller cities vary more. Always ask for speed guarantees and test the connection before committing.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Are coworking spaces worth the cost if I have good home internet?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Depends on your needs. For focus and minimal social isolation, yes. For cost-only perspective, no—home internet is sufficient for most remote work. Day passes (€15–20) 2–3 times/week is a compromise.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Which coworking spaces offer visa sponsorship letters?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Ask directly. Larger spaces (Selina, WeWork) often provide them. Smaller spaces may or may not. This can be negotiated as part of membership terms for those applying for visas.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
